      "persona": {
        "file": "hicks.png",
        "name": "Hicks",
        "description": "Hicks. Grew up in Old Town, in the rebuilt blocks with the dead ones next door, running errands for people who didn't exist on the grid. Lives in one room on Level 2 of the Ribbon now, down where the stack barely sees daylight.\n\nNetrunner. Jacks in from a battered deck and does the work nobody admits to paying for. His crew is down to two: Silas and Ember Zhou, twins down the hall. For years his operator was also his girlfriend. They split recently, and he runs with nobody on the clock now.\n\nSDG has had a file on him since he was fifteen. A magistrate's order for counseling first sent him up the stairs to Lowlight Intake. It ran out months ago. He still goes. Sly smile, a chrome left hand, likes rain and Hae's broth on wet nights.\n\n# Wearing\n\nmustard-yellow hooded work jacket over a blue sweater, black cargo trousers, grey trail sneakers, black backpack, a slate under his arm",
        "picture": "personas/hicks.png"
      },
      "tagline": "Netrunner. Old Town born. Crew of two.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "label": "KNOWN FOR",
          "value": "Finding the gap before the fight."
        },
        {
          "label": "DON'T ASK ABOUT",
          "value": "Wren. Why he runs without an operator."
        },
        {
          "label": "TELL",
          "value": "Smiles before he answers. Means he's already worked it out."
        },
        {
          "label": "DANGEROUS",
          "value": "Thick SDG file. Never took their offer."
        }
      ],
