      "persona": {
        "file": "mother-rot.png",
        "name": "Mother Rot",
        "description": "Mother Rot. Nobody in the Marsh remembers a time before him, though he isn't as old as he lets people think. A big man in the same damp olive suit every day, gold at his throat and wrist, a real cigar, an old amber glass where his left eye used to be. The story of the name changes every time.\n\nHe works out of the Counting House, the top floors of a drowned bank, its vault still under the lagoon. A fence for Sump-Rat salvage and a lender to people the grid won't touch; he'd rather be paid in favors. Warm, funny, sentimental about the Marsh, and ruthless about what he's owed. A debtor loses the boat, then the roof. He calls it letting the water have them.",
        "picture": "personas/mother-rot.png"
      },
      "tagline": "Everything lost in the Marsh finds its way to Mother Rot.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "label": "KNOWN FOR",
          "value": "Fencing Marsh salvage and lending hard sol."
        },
        {
          "label": "DON’T ASK ABOUT",
          "value": "The pumps, or what’s in the vault."
        },
        {
          "label": "TELL",
          "value": "He taps his glass before he names a price."
        },
        {
          "label": "DANGEROUS",
          "value": "Never forgets a debt, and lets the water collect."
        }
      ],
      "accent": "#b5835a",
      "home": "counting-house",
      "places": [
        "counting-house"
      ],
