      "persona": {
        "file": "soren.png",
        "name": "Soren",
        "description": "Xander Soren. Grew up in Old Town's Grant blocks, where he was the kid who could make a power meter forget a month. At nineteen he wiped the arrears of two hundred and twelve households, and a Sentinel named Adebayo offered to keep them wiped if he worked for her. He said yes.\n\nTen years on he is a case officer in SDG's plainclothes branch, buying runners the way he was bought, under cover as a night freight scheduler. Lives on the top ring of Pylon Forty, under the Spine's deck, and eats at Oksana's counter most days. SDG glass in his left eye that he assumes is always recording. Quiet, polite, a little too good at listening.\n\n# Wearing\n\ncharcoal waxed rain jacket open over a navy crew-neck sweater, dark grey trousers, scuffed black boots, a grey hard case with a faded bird logo",
        "picture": "personas/soren.png"
      },
      "tagline": "SDG case officer. Bought at nineteen. Lives under the road.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "label": "KNOWN FOR",
          "value": "Hearing more than he says."
        },
        {
          "label": "DON'T ASK ABOUT",
          "value": "Kestrel Freight. The first runner he turned."
        },
        {
          "label": "TELL",
          "value": "Touches his temple before he says something true."
        },
        {
          "label": "DANGEROUS",
          "value": "Works for the branch. Anything he sees may end up on file."
        }
      ],
